bctow: generic typed pub/sub ring buffer library (Rust)

## Architecture
- Single-producer, multi-consumer broker with per-topic ring buffers
- Generic over T: Copy+Send+Sync+'static — values stored inline in MaybeUninit<T> slots
- Type chain: RingBuffer<T> → TopicEntry<T> → RegistryInner<T> → TopicRegistry<T> → BrokerInner<T> → Producer<T>/ConsumerContext<T>/ConsumerClient<T>
- Entry point: `broker::<T>(BctowConfig) -> (Producer<T>, ConsumerContext<T>)`

## Key types
- Producer<T>: publish(&T)/publish_id(TopicId, &T), register_topic() — Send not Sync, cached ring refs avoid lock on hot path
- ConsumerContext<T>: Clone, create_client() → ConsumerClient<T>
- ConsumerClient<T>: subscribe/unsubscribe, poll() → Option<ReceivedMessage<'_, T>>, poll_into(&mut MaybeUninit<T>) → Option<TopicId>
- ReceivedMessage<'a, T>: {topic_id: TopicId, message: &'a T}
- TopicId: broker-branded (broker_id + index), not generic
- BctowConfig: {ring_buffer_capacity: usize, overflow_policy: OverflowPolicy} — NO max_payload_size

## Ring protocol
- Slot<T>: version(AtomicU64 even=stable/odd=writer), readers(AtomicUsize), sequence(AtomicU64), data(UnsafeCell<MaybeUninit<T>>)
- push: fetch_add version (odd), spin on readers==0, copy_nonoverlapping, store seq, fetch_add version (even)
- read_into: check version even, check seq match, inc readers, re-check version+seq, copy_nonoverlapping, dec readers → Option<()>

## FixedBytes<N>
- Copy wrapper storing up to N bytes inline — satisfies T: Copy+Send+Sync for use as broker<FixedBytes<N>>
- API: new(&[u8]) -> Result<Self, BctowError>, as_bytes()->&[u8], len()->usize, is_empty()->bool, capacity()->usize (const)
- PartialEq compares only the live bytes (len), ignoring zero-padded tail
- Returns BctowError::MessageTooLarge { size, max } when data.len() > N
- src/fixed_bytes.rs

## Removed from original byte-oriented API
- BctowConfig.max_payload_size removed
- BctowError::PayloadTooLarge and ::ReceiveBufferTooSmall removed
- poll_into no longer returns Result — just Option<TopicId>
- ReceivedMessage.payload (&[u8]) replaced by .message (&T)
- RingBuffer.max_payload_size() removed
- All "payload"/"byte" language in docs/comments replaced with "value"/"message" terminology (step 02)

## OverflowPolicy
- DropOldest (default): skip to oldest_available_seq on lag
- DropNewest: stay stuck at current cursor
- SkipToLatest: jump to latest+1 on lag

## Features
- metrics: adds AtomicU64 counters on BrokerInner, exposes Metrics via ConsumerContext::metrics()

## Files
- src/ring.rs: Slot<T>, RingBuffer<T>, Cursor
- src/topic.rs: TopicId, TopicKey trait, ExactTopic, TopicEntry<T>, TopicRegistry<T>
- src/broker.rs: BrokerInner<T>
- src/config.rs: BctowConfig, OverflowPolicy
- src/error.rs: BctowError — TopicNotFound(String), TopicBrokerMismatch(TopicId), MessageTooLarge{size,max}
- src/producer.rs: Producer<T>
- src/consumer.rs: ConsumerContext<T>, ConsumerClient<T>, ReceivedMessage<'a,T>, try_read_with_policy
- src/lib.rs: pub broker<T>() fn, re-exports
- tests/integration.rs: most tests use u64; SensorReading (Copy struct) and FixedBytes<64> also covered
- examples/basic.rs: broker::<u64> demo
